From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: lzma: fix Clang 20 WERROR failures

The imported LZMA SDK uses a generic void pointer as the match-finder
callback context and casts implementations taking CMatchFinder pointers
into that interface. Clang 20 diagnoses these intentional casts with
-Wcast-function-type-strict, which becomes fatal under CONFIG_WERROR.

Disable only that diagnostic for LzFind.o. Keep the global WERROR policy
and all other Clang diagnostics intact.

Also fix an over-indented unconditional block (-Wmisleading-indentation) and
replace an unused-argument self-assignment with a void cast in the encoder
(-Wself-assign). Both become fatal under CONFIG_WERROR.

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
 lib/lzma/LzmaEnc.c | 4 ++--
 lib/lzma/Makefile  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/lib/lzma/Makefile
+++ b/lib/lzma/Makefile
@@ -5,3 +5,4 @@ lzma_decompress-objs := LzmaDec.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_LZMA_DECOMPRESS) += lzma_decompress.o
 
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Iinclude/linux -Iinclude/linux/lzma -include types.h
+CFLAGS_LzFind.o += $(call cc-disable-warning, cast-function-type-strict)
--- a/lib/lzma/LzmaEnc.c
+++ b/lib/lzma/LzmaEnc.c
@@ -1342,6 +1342,6 @@
         startLen = lenTest + 1;

       /* if (_maxMode) */
-        {
+      {
           UInt32 lenTest2 = lenTest + 1;
           UInt32 limit = lenTest2 + p->numFastBytes;
@@ -2081,7 +2081,7 @@ static void LzmaEnc_Finish(CLzmaEncHandl
   if (p->mtMode)
     MatchFinderMt_ReleaseStream(&p->matchFinderMt);
   #else
-  pp = pp;
+  (void)pp;
   #endif
 }
 
